WEBVTT

00:01.250 --> 00:04.340
Good work on your 
competition entries, everyone!

00:04.340 --> 00:06.170
Good work!

00:06.170 --> 00:07.290
Who's up for round two?!

00:07.290 --> 00:07.980
Me!

00:08.670 --> 00:10.810
Senpai, do you want to 
walk to the station toge—

00:10.810 --> 00:12.080
Shinozaki-san...

00:12.930 --> 00:14.490
Once we're done...

00:14.900 --> 00:18.490
would you like to come do 
something naughty with your senpai?

00:18.920 --> 00:20.750
<i>Something naughty?!</i>

00:21.820 --> 00:24.120
<i>There's a senpai where I work...</i>

00:24.660 --> 00:29.450
<i>who's tiny and sexy—I mean... cute.</i>

00:31.000 --> 00:32.510
Here you go!

00:32.840 --> 00:34.510
Time to eat!

00:34.960 --> 00:38.300
After having some drinks... late at night...

00:38.890 --> 00:43.410
I know it's bad for you, 
but I can't resist the sweet siren call...

00:44.060 --> 00:44.940
of ramen!

00:44.940 --> 00:46.870
<i>That's what she meant?!</i>

00:46.870 --> 00:49.570
What's wrong? Aren't you going to eat?

00:49.570 --> 00:52.940
It's just... I didn't expect ramen.

00:53.110 --> 00:55.740
What did you expect, then?

00:56.410 --> 01:00.030
<i>Is she doing this on purpose, 
or accidentally?!</i>

01:00.030 --> 01:03.290
<b>Stray Ramen</b>

01:01.300 --> 01:03.290
Thanks for coming!

01:03.810 --> 01:05.790
Thank you for treating me.

01:05.790 --> 01:09.130
You worked really hard on your contest entry.

01:09.130 --> 01:12.300
It's not much, but I wanted to 
reward you, as your senpai.

01:13.020 --> 01:14.290
<i>Senpai...</i>

01:15.420 --> 01:20.300
<i>She's nice and always looking out for me.</i>

01:20.860 --> 01:23.150
<i>And that makes me so happy, but...</i>

01:24.420 --> 01:30.090
<i>Are we always just going to be 
senpai and kohai?</i>

01:30.770 --> 01:32.420
Man, I am starving!

01:32.420 --> 01:34.980
Y'know what they say about ramen?

01:32.980 --> 01:33.980
Um...

01:34.980 --> 01:38.410
If someone craves ramen late at night, 
they've got a strong libido.

01:38.410 --> 01:41.060
What the heck? Like they're not satisfied?

01:41.060 --> 01:42.210
Yep, exactly.

01:45.580 --> 01:49.340
I was really just looking 
for some refreshing tea!

01:49.340 --> 01:52.360
R-Right! Tea! I get it!

01:52.360 --> 01:55.010
Anyway! You were about to say something?!

01:55.010 --> 01:57.310
I-It can wait until some other time!

01:58.400 --> 02:05.080
<i>Oh, I love you so much, I just have to laugh</i>

02:09.940 --> 02:14.700
My Tiny Senpai

02:15.440 --> 02:17.780
<i>We've got an emergency here</i>

02:18.200 --> 02:20.560
<i>Are you paying attention, me?</i>

02:20.950 --> 02:26.790
<i>There's someone other than me 
dancing around inside of my heart</i>

02:26.790 --> 02:29.040
<i>I want to talk to her</i>

02:29.540 --> 02:32.080
<i>I want to touch her</i>

02:32.080 --> 02:37.580
<i>Look, I get it, but for now try to pipe down</i>

02:38.090 --> 02:40.800
<i>What in the world am I doing?</i>

02:40.800 --> 02:43.550
<i>You're right next to me</i>

02:43.550 --> 02:49.810
<i>And this is the perfect chance...</i>

02:50.560 --> 02:51.390
<i>HONEY</i>

02:51.390 --> 02:56.100
<i>I'm trapped by that sweet rich taste</i>

02:56.100 --> 02:59.310
<i>And I don't think I can ever escape</i>

02:59.310 --> 03:01.810
<i>I may as well just sink into it</i>

03:01.810 --> 03:02.640
<i>HONEY</i>

03:02.640 --> 03:07.410
<i>It's another day in your dazzling presence</i>

03:07.630 --> 03:10.410
<i>We may never be 
on the same page with this love but</i>

03:10.410 --> 03:16.850
<i>Oh, I love you so much, I just have to laugh</i>

03:28.470 --> 03:32.980
#12 A Story About the Tiny Senpai Where I Work

03:28.980 --> 03:31.730
Hayakawa-san, you headed for lunch?

03:32.550 --> 03:34.230
Mind if I join you?

03:35.150 --> 03:39.830
<i>My boss at my job... is pleasant 
and friendly to everyone.</i>

03:40.490 --> 03:42.200
Okay... sure.

03:42.200 --> 03:43.590
What's this?

03:43.990 --> 03:48.590
Going to lunch together... 
Is this a lunch date?

03:51.170 --> 03:52.380
N-No!

03:52.380 --> 03:54.250
Yep, yep! Let's call it a date!

03:55.390 --> 03:57.370
Don't say something like that at the office!

03:57.370 --> 04:00.010
What if people start spreading weird rumors?!

04:00.710 --> 04:02.780
Considering it's you, Hayakawa-san, 
I wouldn't mind.

04:08.510 --> 04:10.210
<i>Wh-Wh-Wh-What's that mean?!</i>

04:10.210 --> 04:13.580
<i>Considering who said it, 
it's probably nothing significant, but...</i>

04:14.350 --> 04:17.690
Ugh! You just had to 
say something, Katase-san!

04:18.980 --> 04:19.690
Senpai!

04:20.380 --> 04:22.320
I found my wallet, so let's go.

04:22.320 --> 04:23.600
It's a date!

04:23.600 --> 04:25.370
It's not!

04:27.300 --> 04:28.720
Zakishino!

04:28.200 --> 04:31.950
<b>Rainbow Sweet Potato Tarts</b>

04:28.720 --> 04:31.950
<i>Mensore</i>! Here's some Okinawa stuff.

04:31.950 --> 04:33.450
Thanks.

04:34.080 --> 04:36.210
Did you enjoy the resort?

04:36.590 --> 04:39.890
Are you hitting on me? 
Aw, but I've got a girlfriend!

04:39.890 --> 04:40.710
<i>Ugh...</i>

04:41.140 --> 04:44.610
I was transferred, 
but I used my paid time off, Yuri-tan!

04:44.610 --> 04:46.600
I'm so glad, Masa-tan!

04:46.600 --> 04:48.350
<i>Who even does that?</i>

04:48.350 --> 04:51.500
It was... a real blast...

04:51.850 --> 04:55.260
Console me, Zakishino!

04:55.260 --> 04:56.850
Shinozaki-san!

04:57.210 --> 05:00.110
Could I bug you for a bit after work?

05:01.860 --> 05:04.610
<b>40th Anniversary</b>

05:02.780 --> 05:04.610
A Meowtaro game?

05:04.900 --> 05:09.870
Yep! My anthropomorphized 
hottie Meowtaro game is finished!

05:06.860 --> 05:09.870
<b>Doki Doki
Meowtaro
</b>~Our Academy of Romance~

05:06.860 --> 05:09.870
Start

05:11.170 --> 05:13.360
It's finally done!

05:13.360 --> 05:14.500
And so...

05:14.970 --> 05:19.130
I was hoping to have Shinozaki 
the gamer play it for a bit!

05:19.490 --> 05:21.820
Well, let's get to it, then.

05:21.820 --> 05:22.660
Yeah.

05:23.130 --> 05:27.130
Out Front of School

05:23.130 --> 05:27.130
Meowtaro: {and then the below dialog}

05:23.370 --> 05:27.130
Hey there. I'm Meowtaro. Nice to meet you.

05:27.810 --> 05:31.140
So you try to romance Meowtaro 
from the perspective of a girl?

05:31.540 --> 05:33.050
Looks like it.

05:34.140 --> 05:39.060
I hear you're quite the cook. 
I'd love to try something you've made.

05:34.140 --> 05:41.650
Restaurant

05:34.140 --> 05:41.650
<b>Meat</b>

05:34.140 --> 05:41.650
<b>Fish</b>

05:34.140 --> 05:41.650
<b>Vegetables</b>

05:34.140 --> 05:41.650
<b>Fruit</b>

05:34.140 --> 05:41.650
Affection

05:34.140 --> 05:41.650
Meowtaro:

05:39.510 --> 05:41.650
You've gotta pick the menu...?

05:42.070 --> 05:45.580
Even if he's anthropomorphized, 
Meowtaro's a cat.

05:45.580 --> 05:48.080
He probably likes fish, right?

05:48.080 --> 05:49.500
Probably!

05:49.870 --> 05:51.610
Fish it is, then.

05:52.030 --> 05:55.540
<b>Fish</b>

05:52.030 --> 05:55.540
Affection

05:52.030 --> 05:55.660
Fish, huh? That's not bad, but...

05:52.030 --> 05:56.160
Meowtaro:

05:52.030 --> 05:57.920
Restaurant

05:55.660 --> 05:56.400
Huh?

05:56.400 --> 05:58.490
That wasn't the reaction 
I was expecting.

05:59.030 --> 06:01.570
Meowtaro is the heir to a major corporation.

06:01.970 --> 06:04.370
He eats fish every day, so he's tired of it!

06:04.370 --> 06:06.800
I don't think that's part of the backstory...

06:07.290 --> 06:09.550
The best choice is fruit!

06:09.550 --> 06:15.310
Restaurant

06:09.550 --> 06:15.310
<b>Fruit</b>

06:09.550 --> 06:15.310
Affection

06:09.550 --> 06:15.310
Meowtaro:

06:09.890 --> 06:11.820
I've never had anything like it...

06:11.820 --> 06:15.310
You must know about a world 
I'm unfamiliar with.

06:15.910 --> 06:17.300
What does that even mean?

06:17.300 --> 06:19.130
What are you all doing?

06:20.190 --> 06:21.500
Kurusu-san.

06:21.500 --> 06:23.370
Office hours are over.

06:24.090 --> 06:25.820
Why are you all here?

06:26.120 --> 06:30.570
I was having them try out 
the Meowtaro game I made.

06:30.910 --> 06:32.830
Want to try it, Kurusu-san?

06:33.260 --> 06:35.330
A Meowtaro game?!

06:35.330 --> 06:39.330
I do! I want to play! Please let me play it!

06:39.330 --> 06:41.330
Meowtaro:

06:39.330 --> 06:41.330
I could steal these lips
in a heartbeat.

06:40.050 --> 06:41.330
This is it...

06:42.340 --> 06:43.340
Who?

06:43.340 --> 06:46.290
This is anthropomorphic hottie Meowtaro!

06:46.770 --> 06:50.090
It'll let us develop 
the latent otome game market!

06:50.430 --> 06:53.050
<i>Meowtaro...? Hot...? Anthropomorphic...?</i>

06:53.050 --> 06:55.850
My Meowtaro... what in the world...?

06:56.160 --> 06:59.210
This isn't development. It's pandering.

06:59.210 --> 07:02.850
It doesn't convey a fraction of 
Meowtaro's actual appeal.

07:03.380 --> 07:07.110
It's more likely to chase off 
existing fans than develop new ones.

07:07.530 --> 07:08.990
It's idiocy.

07:08.990 --> 07:12.220
Do you really think we can 
open up new opportunities

07:12.220 --> 07:14.860
by being so beholden to old fans 
that we never try anything new?

07:14.860 --> 07:16.700
It's a question of methodology.

07:16.700 --> 07:20.100
This would honestly be better off 
as a completely distinct project...

07:18.260 --> 07:20.620
Let's keep on playing, Zakishino!

07:20.620 --> 07:25.880
Roof

07:20.620 --> 07:25.880
Affection

07:20.620 --> 07:25.880
Meowtaro:

07:20.620 --> 07:25.880
The culture festival is ending...
There's something I need to tell to you.

07:26.300 --> 07:29.050
Are we gonna get a confession 
after the festival?!

07:29.050 --> 07:32.540
I'm not sure. It feels a little too soon 
for things to be ending...

07:32.540 --> 07:35.140
But it's a private meeting on the rooftop!

07:35.630 --> 07:37.140
<i>On the rooftop...</i>

07:37.480 --> 07:39.140
<i>Meeting in private...</i>

07:41.690 --> 07:43.300
<i>That sounds familiar.</i>

07:43.650 --> 07:47.770
Roof

07:43.650 --> 07:47.770
Affection

07:43.650 --> 07:47.770
Meowtaro:

07:44.020 --> 07:47.770
Let's always be good senpai and kohai, okay?

07:48.330 --> 07:49.780
<i>This line...</i>

07:50.290 --> 07:51.780
<i>That line...</i>

07:51.780 --> 07:55.780
Let's always be good coworkers, okay?

07:56.120 --> 07:57.780
<i>It's kinda similar!</i>

07:58.180 --> 08:01.930
Aw, man, we got rejected before the confession.

08:03.650 --> 08:05.010
Rejected...

08:05.790 --> 08:07.040
Before confessing...

08:07.580 --> 08:09.210
Rejected?

08:10.210 --> 08:11.630
Before confessing...?

08:12.050 --> 08:15.730
<i>I rejected him?! 
That's not what I was trying to do...!</i>

08:15.730 --> 08:19.560
<i>Is that what Shinozaki-san felt at the time?!</i>

08:19.560 --> 08:22.920
<i>I really was rejected?! 
That's what really happened?!</i>

08:22.920 --> 08:27.060
<i>And after I had tried to forget all about it!</i>

08:28.660 --> 08:30.320
What's with you two?

08:31.970 --> 08:35.200
Hold it right there. It's too soon to give up.

08:35.490 --> 08:38.200
I know you two must have realized it.

08:38.550 --> 08:42.200
There's still a while before the ending, 
and you haven't confessed yet...

08:42.520 --> 08:46.490
So you can still seal the deal yet! 
Your chance is still out there...

08:46.490 --> 08:47.710
Or do you mean to tell me...

08:48.350 --> 08:51.840
that you two don't love Meowtaro that much?!

08:52.180 --> 08:53.970
I mean, we don't.

08:54.870 --> 08:56.310
<i>Hadn't confessed yet...</i>

08:56.860 --> 08:58.850
<i>There's still a chance...</i>

08:59.630 --> 09:01.010
<i>I hadn't confessed yet!</i>

09:01.790 --> 09:03.610
<i>There's still a chance!</i>

09:04.350 --> 09:07.300
That's right! We haven't been rejected yet!

09:07.300 --> 09:09.140
I agree!

09:09.140 --> 09:12.220
Is there a reason you guys are so into this?

09:12.220 --> 09:15.110
It's not even the real Meowtaro.

09:15.930 --> 09:18.260
That video game was fun.

09:18.260 --> 09:19.620
It sure was.

09:19.620 --> 09:22.680
I liked how they ended up 
together in the end.

09:22.680 --> 09:23.620
Yeah.

09:26.490 --> 09:27.940
Shinozaki-san.

09:28.630 --> 09:33.380
What was it that you wanted to tell me before?

09:41.810 --> 09:49.100
I was wondering if we'd always 
just be a senpai and a kohai.

09:56.610 --> 10:04.700
I remember saying that we should always 
just be good coworkers before.

10:05.780 --> 10:07.210
But now...

10:10.180 --> 10:13.850
Maybe now, it'd be okay if things changed.

10:16.720 --> 10:20.130
Like, for instance...

10:20.940 --> 10:23.370
We... We...

10:23.720 --> 10:26.700
We could be... friends.

10:31.400 --> 10:33.760
I mean, we already get along well, but—

10:33.760 --> 10:34.780
Does that mean...

10:36.170 --> 10:40.820
Does that mean you wouldn't mind if we spent 
more time together in our personal lives?

10:43.710 --> 10:44.830
Yes.

10:45.560 --> 10:47.540
I can invite you out shopping?

10:47.540 --> 10:48.520
Sure!

10:48.520 --> 10:50.540
And for lunch on days off?

10:50.540 --> 10:53.340
If anything, I'd think that's 
a natural thing for friends to do!

10:53.650 --> 10:57.590
A-And if I send you a text asking 
"Are you busy?" for no reason...

10:57.940 --> 11:00.090
We're friends, so it's not a problem!

11:00.380 --> 11:03.100
We could send pictures of us wearing 
new clothes we've bought!

11:03.100 --> 11:06.720
That sounds like the kind of thing 
friends should do together!

11:09.190 --> 11:11.480
Because we're friends!

11:18.020 --> 11:19.080
We're friends!

11:19.080 --> 11:20.190
Yes, we are!

11:20.740 --> 11:24.700
<i>And so they've obtained the new 
rationalization... of friendship.</i>

11:24.700 --> 11:29.440
H-Hang on, Manager! Don't turn into 
sugar and blow away again!

11:25.830 --> 11:29.440
Sugar!

11:30.370 --> 11:33.530
<i>My Tiny Senpai</i>.

11:36.040 --> 11:42.010
<b>Sunpick 40th Anniversary</b>

11:37.010 --> 11:39.900
<i>My Tiny Senpai</i>!

11:39.900 --> 11:41.210
Yeah!

11:45.670 --> 11:46.700
Senpai!

11:48.380 --> 11:49.690
Good morning.

11:49.690 --> 11:51.130
Good morning.

11:52.630 --> 11:54.270
<i>Senpai and I...</i>

11:55.060 --> 11:56.630
<i>Shinozaki-san and I...</i>

11:58.500 --> 12:00.350
<i>are friends now.</i>

12:01.530 --> 12:05.030
<b>Product Development</b>

12:01.530 --> 12:05.030
<b>Group 2</b>

12:02.450 --> 12:05.030
<i>Not just coworkers...</i>

12:05.340 --> 12:07.590
<i>But a personal relationship, too.</i>

12:10.090 --> 12:11.540
I've uploaded the data.

12:11.930 --> 12:14.130
Okay. Let me just confirm it.

12:16.830 --> 12:19.110
<i>Senpai and I are friends now.</i>

12:19.930 --> 12:22.330
<i>Shinozaki-san and I are friends now.</i>

12:23.190 --> 12:24.190
<i>And yet...</i>

12:24.800 --> 12:26.170
<i>And yet...</i>

12:27.250 --> 12:29.680
<i>Nothing's changed!</i>

12:29.680 --> 12:33.440
<i>I want to take her out for dinner or something 
 outside work, but don't know when to ask!</i>

12:33.440 --> 12:36.480
<i>I bought new clothes 
and even took selfies in them!</i>

12:36.480 --> 12:38.440
<i>But I don't know when 
I should send them!</i>

12:38.440 --> 12:41.440
<i>I mean, I've never had a female friend before!</i>

12:41.440 --> 12:44.700
<i>I mean, I've never had a male friend before!</i>

12:45.130 --> 12:47.450
<i>How exactly do I do anything?!</i>

12:47.450 --> 12:50.450
<i>I don't know how to do anything!</i>

12:51.390 --> 12:52.700
<i>If only we had...</i>

12:53.090 --> 12:54.960
<i>If only we had...</i>

12:57.260 --> 12:59.970
<i>even the slightest new development...</i>

13:02.460 --> 13:04.690
Sounds like Okinawa was pretty rough.

13:04.690 --> 13:11.220
Tell me about it. Everywhere 
I turned, people were in heat...

13:09.060 --> 13:12.880
Is it all right that I'm joining for lunch?

13:12.880 --> 13:16.860
Sure. We should get together
for lunch every now and then.

13:16.860 --> 13:19.070
Th-Thank you.

13:20.170 --> 13:24.370
<i>I want to make something happen, 
but I'm not sure how to approach it...</i>

13:25.090 --> 13:29.610
<i>I want to make something happen, 
but I'm not sure how to approach it...</i>

13:30.620 --> 13:32.110
<i>The timing...</i>

13:32.740 --> 13:36.010
Still, I'm sure getting 
to go to Okinawa was nice.

13:36.010 --> 13:38.180
Are you feeling a bit more refreshed?

13:38.180 --> 13:39.870
I guess a little...

13:41.500 --> 13:45.260
Golden Week is coming up soon, 
so I'd like to go somewhere.

13:45.730 --> 13:48.010
Hey, do any of you have plans?

13:48.010 --> 13:49.580
<i>This timing!</i>

13:50.650 --> 13:53.770
I'm not really doing anything.

13:53.770 --> 13:57.380
But it'd be nice to go out with some friends.

13:55.770 --> 13:57.850
<b>Obvious Bait</b>

13:58.420 --> 14:00.910
Nothing on my end.

14:01.490 --> 14:04.500
But I'd really like to have fun with friends.

14:03.020 --> 14:04.860
<b>Obvious Bait</b>

14:04.860 --> 14:07.420
<i>Now I know they don't have any plans...</i>

14:07.420 --> 14:09.870
I'm not doing jack, either.

14:10.120 --> 14:15.120
I've got some. Every year, I go to 
an amusement park with a friend from high school.

14:15.440 --> 14:16.870
<i>An amusement park?!</i>

14:16.870 --> 14:18.870
We wear matching outfits...

14:19.430 --> 14:22.060
<i>Matching outfits...</i>

14:22.730 --> 14:23.630
<i>Nice!</i>

14:24.130 --> 14:26.630
And then buy merchandise to 
commemorate the occasion...

14:27.470 --> 14:29.260
<i>Commemorative merch...</i>

14:30.220 --> 14:31.130
<i>Nice!</i>

14:32.230 --> 14:34.900
Going to an amusement park sounds fantastic.

14:34.900 --> 14:37.890
It's like friendship utopia.

14:37.890 --> 14:41.560
You think? There are a lot of people 
with their kids, too.

14:41.560 --> 14:45.010
But we're doing something extra this time.

14:45.010 --> 14:46.400
Check this out...

14:46.400 --> 14:49.910
We've reserved a room at the park's hotel!

14:50.160 --> 14:52.160
<i>H-Hotel?!</i>

14:52.160 --> 14:56.160
There's a private lounge with a bar where 
you can look at the park while drinking.

14:56.850 --> 14:59.420
<i>A private lounge with a bar...</i>

15:00.790 --> 15:02.340
Shinozaki-san.

15:03.630 --> 15:05.550
Here's to looking at you, Senpai.

15:08.420 --> 15:11.430
We sit on the bed and talk about the day...

15:12.310 --> 15:13.540
<i>On the bed...</i>

15:15.420 --> 15:16.510
Senpai...

15:17.420 --> 15:19.940
This was a lot of fun, huh?

15:21.690 --> 15:25.940
And then we wrap it up by enjoying 
the room's open air bath!

15:27.990 --> 15:30.490
<i>T-Together...</i>

15:31.330 --> 15:33.950
<i>in a bath?!</i>

15:33.950 --> 15:35.400
And then in the morning...

15:35.400 --> 15:36.790
Yamagishi-san!

15:37.450 --> 15:40.820
Tthat seems a little unsavory, 
even for friends!

15:40.820 --> 15:43.700
That's right! I-I mean, bathing together...

15:43.700 --> 15:45.880
Seems pretty normal to me.

15:45.880 --> 15:47.930
I just think it's a little too soon for that!

15:47.930 --> 15:50.180
Maybe after the relationship's matured some!

15:50.180 --> 15:51.730
You think?

15:51.730 --> 15:53.020
We do!

15:53.020 --> 15:55.540
Oh, wait, are you two...

15:55.540 --> 15:57.970
embarrassed about bathing around others?

16:04.220 --> 16:07.160
I wouldn't say that...

16:07.160 --> 16:09.630
I'd be kind of glad to, actually...

16:08.270 --> 16:11.240
<b>These two are actually lewd</b>

16:11.240 --> 16:14.170
I mean, I've known her since high school, so...

16:14.170 --> 16:16.330
A friend from your school days, huh?

16:16.740 --> 16:18.370
That sounds like a lot of fun.

16:19.050 --> 16:21.940
<i>The hotel took me by surprise, but...</i>

16:21.940 --> 16:24.750
<i>an amusement park... That really sounds nice.</i>

16:25.500 --> 16:28.250
<i>It might be too soon for a hotel, but...</i>

16:28.250 --> 16:30.760
<i>an amusement park? Nice idea.</i>

16:31.220 --> 16:34.370
Talking about it has made me want to go.

16:34.370 --> 16:35.720
Me, too!

16:35.720 --> 16:36.680
In that case...

16:36.680 --> 16:37.740
No.

16:38.800 --> 16:41.850
Theme parks are the domain 
of other characters...

16:42.270 --> 16:47.380
Money earned from Meowtaro... 
can't be spent on others... ever.

16:48.370 --> 16:50.930
Do you not like amusement parks, Kurusu-san?

16:50.930 --> 16:52.140
It's not that.

16:52.530 --> 16:56.530
Meowtaro Land Project Outline

16:53.060 --> 16:55.260
I wanna make Meowtaro Land.

16:55.260 --> 16:56.530
So if anything, you love them.

16:56.980 --> 16:58.420
In that case, shouldn't you

16:58.420 --> 17:00.910
check other places out 
as a way of gathering intel?

17:02.350 --> 17:04.660
Instead of trying to make 
something from scratch,

17:04.660 --> 17:07.890
it'd be a good idea to use 
a successful model as reference.

17:07.890 --> 17:09.610
It'll help you come up 
with unique ideas, too.

17:10.170 --> 17:11.350
That's a fair point.

17:12.160 --> 17:15.680
In that case, since it's come up, 
why don't we all go during Golden Week?

17:16.230 --> 17:17.550
<i>All of us...</i>

17:18.140 --> 17:19.650
That sounds good.

17:20.360 --> 17:22.310
Let's all go together!

17:22.310 --> 17:25.820
Okay, then! If we're all going, I wanna go, too!

17:25.820 --> 17:27.260
So, when should we do it?

17:27.260 --> 17:28.910
Let's see...

17:29.810 --> 17:31.820
<b>May</b>

17:29.810 --> 17:31.820
<b>Sunday         Monday        Tuesday      Wednesday     Thursday         Friday           Saturday</b>

17:29.810 --> 17:31.820
Hayakawa X
Katase X

17:29.810 --> 17:31.820
Shinozaki X

17:29.810 --> 17:31.820
Yamagishi ♀ X
Hayakawa X

17:29.810 --> 17:31.820
Yamagishi ♂ X
Kurusu X

17:32.270 --> 17:34.350
I guess our schedules don't match up...

17:34.690 --> 17:38.170
Guess we won't be able 
to all go during Golden Week.

17:39.050 --> 17:43.330
Well, what about during summer vacation, then?

17:43.330 --> 17:45.740
Since there's more time until then,

17:45.740 --> 17:48.140
it should be easier 
to make our schedules match.

17:48.140 --> 17:50.260
It's on hold, then.

17:54.430 --> 17:57.590
I wanted to go to that amusement park...

17:58.630 --> 17:59.690
Senpai!

18:01.170 --> 18:02.730
Shinozaki-san...

18:04.990 --> 18:09.390
U-Um, I know the scheduling 
didn't work out for everyone, but...

18:12.020 --> 18:13.990
Would you... well...

18:17.270 --> 18:21.090
as friends... we could...

18:23.870 --> 18:29.080
What Yamagishi-san was talking about 
sounded nice! So... maybe...

18:29.330 --> 18:30.580
The amusement park.

18:33.420 --> 18:36.300
Let's go to the amusement park together.

18:46.180 --> 18:47.060
Yeah!

18:48.890 --> 18:52.140
You said you were always free.

18:52.140 --> 18:54.570
But then you had a day 
where you couldn't... Why?

18:54.570 --> 18:58.150
Well, let's just chalk it up 
to doing the bro thing.

19:04.410 --> 19:06.550
The cute shoes I bought

19:07.070 --> 19:09.500
or the sneakers I've broken in...

19:17.920 --> 19:20.430
Picking the right look for visiting an amusement park with that special someone
Share    Tweet    Like

19:20.760 --> 19:21.620
Okay!

19:26.700 --> 19:28.700
The fashionable look...

19:29.510 --> 19:31.230
Or the casual one...

19:32.150 --> 19:34.220
Which should I go with?

19:34.220 --> 19:35.500
You got a date?

19:35.940 --> 19:38.350
Don't just show up like that!

19:38.350 --> 19:44.420
You  always spend Golden Week every year 
back at home, but this year you didn't.

19:44.820 --> 19:46.700
So I came to check on you.

19:47.110 --> 19:50.210
I see... a date with Shiorin, then.

19:50.210 --> 19:54.460
It's not a date! We're just going to 
the amusement park together!

19:54.780 --> 19:57.090
Sounds like... a date.

19:57.090 --> 19:58.600
Well, it's not!

19:58.600 --> 20:01.020
I haven't confessed to her 
or started going out!

20:01.020 --> 20:04.090
We're really just going as friends!

20:04.530 --> 20:05.490
Then, you think...

20:06.090 --> 20:08.850
going to an amusement park 
is something that friends do?

20:08.850 --> 20:10.580
Y-Yeah.

20:14.150 --> 20:17.610
<b>Amusement Park Gate</b>

20:14.620 --> 20:17.610
<i>Amusement Park Gate, Amusement Park Gate.</i>

20:24.060 --> 20:26.580
<i>I got here faster than I expected.</i>

20:26.580 --> 20:28.740
<i>Maybe I should find a café...</i>

20:31.510 --> 20:33.690
I guess we were on the same train.

20:34.270 --> 20:35.330
<i>Cute!</i>

20:35.630 --> 20:38.010
I woke up a bit early.

20:38.010 --> 20:40.130
M-Me, too.

20:41.050 --> 20:43.130
You seem different from usual.

20:44.460 --> 20:47.370
Your hair's up, and you're wearing pants.

20:49.110 --> 20:51.770
Well, it's an amusement park...

20:51.770 --> 20:54.480
I figured we'd be walking a lot...

20:54.480 --> 20:57.020
I've got sneakers on, too.

20:57.360 --> 20:59.020
So do I.

20:59.400 --> 21:03.530
We'll probably be walking more than 
some hiking trips, honestly.

21:05.940 --> 21:07.530
Yeah!

21:08.390 --> 21:10.540
We're a little early, but let's get in line.

21:11.410 --> 21:12.700
Let's!

21:25.140 --> 21:27.660
<i>There's a senpai where I work...</i>

21:27.660 --> 21:29.490
<i>who is tiny and cute.</i>

21:36.100 --> 21:37.870
I guess we should head home.

21:38.940 --> 21:40.060
I guess so.

21:41.230 --> 21:43.110
But first...

21:44.570 --> 21:47.280
How about it? 
Something to remember the occasion.

21:48.410 --> 21:51.810
I-It's been a while since I've been 
to an amusement park with a friend!

21:51.810 --> 21:53.020
Do you not want to?

21:53.020 --> 21:54.540
I didn't say that!

21:54.860 --> 21:56.080
Want me to take it for you?

21:56.080 --> 21:57.290
Thank you so—

21:57.290 --> 21:58.720
Manager?!

21:58.720 --> 22:01.790
Along with my sister and Hayakawa?! 
Why are you here?!

22:02.130 --> 22:05.380
Li'l bro, you said as much yourself.

22:05.380 --> 22:08.370
Amusement parks are for visiting with your friends.

22:08.810 --> 22:09.800
And thus...

22:10.190 --> 22:13.210
Chihiro, let's go to the amusement park!

22:13.210 --> 22:15.120
Let's invite Hayakawa-san, too, then.

22:15.120 --> 22:17.310
Huh? The amusement park?

22:17.850 --> 22:21.560
And so, the three of us had a great time.

22:19.170 --> 22:20.890
Why am I here...?

22:21.930 --> 22:23.970
I... see.

22:23.970 --> 22:26.310
Okay, now get closer together!

22:31.950 --> 22:35.450
Shiorin! Shiorin!

22:33.250 --> 22:35.450
Hayakawa-san, did you enjoy yourself?

22:35.450 --> 22:37.730
Well... I guess I did.

22:37.980 --> 22:40.910
<i>Things got kind of busy 
at the end there, but...</i>

22:38.460 --> 22:40.150
Thinking of coming again?

22:40.610 --> 22:41.970
I guess I am.
